                <pb facs="0609" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg521"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Garrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February 10,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay instructs Mr. Garrett to consult the Netherlands Government in regard to
                    the possibility and desirability of an arrangement between the neutral powers to
                    use their good offices with Russia and Japan for the purpose of inducing them to
                    respect China’s neutrality and administrative entity as far as possible,
                    limiting and localizing the area of hostile operations to minimize the
                    disturbance and excitement of the Chinese people and the injury to commerce and
                    to the peaceful intercourse of the world. If no opposition to this proposition
                    is offered, he is instructed to suggest that the representatives of the
                    Netherlands at St. Petersburg, Tokyo, and Peking be instructed in this
                    sense.)</p>
            </div>
